## [ENT-001] | 2026-07-30 13:44 UTC | Ava | research | ref: research/reports/crewai-integration-assessment.md | see: 20260730T134244Z
Researched CrewAI multi-agent orchestration framework for potential
integration with Suggi-Workstation GitHub org. Key sources: CrewAI
official docs, third-party pricing analyses (CostBench, ComparEdge,
UsagePricing), architectural deep-dives (Codexpedite, PyShine).
Wrote crewai-integration-assessment.md (351 lines) to research/reports/.
Findings: CrewAI uses dual-abstraction model (Crews for collaboration,
Flows for orchestration). GitHub integration exists but requires
Enterprise AMP (free tier hard-capped at 50 execs/month unusable for
automation). OSS self-hosted path (MIT, free) is viable on VPS.
Ava and Link can be modeled as CrewAI Agents but cannot be imported --
OpenClaw-native tooling (memory, wiki, browser, gates) would need
reimplementation. Two-framework stack (Python CrewAI + Node.js OpenClaw)
adds complexity without solving a clear current bottleneck.
Recommendation: monitor, do not adopt now.
